<figure
  class="process-diagram"
  aria-label="Cribra processing pipeline and application-controlled paths"
>
  <ol class="pipeline" role="list" aria-label="Common processing pipeline">
    <li><span>Caller-provided input</span><span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"></span></li>
    <li><span>Detection</span><span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"></span></li>
    <li><span>Validation</span><span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"></span></li>
    <li class="results"><span>Structured results</span></li>
  </ol>

  <div class="branching">
    <p class="choices-label" id="application-paths-label">
      Your application chooses the paths it needs:
    </p>
    <ul class="application-paths" role="list" aria-labelledby="application-paths-label">
      <li>
        <h3>Inspect</h3>
        <p>Findings, classifications, and reports.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Review</h3>
        <p>Candidates, when present, requiring explicit decisions.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Transform</h3>
        <p>
          Explicitly select a <a href="/docs/transformations/">supported transformation</a> to produce
          derived output.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Share</h3>
        <p>
          Explicitly prepare an in-memory Share Bundle using the <a
            href="/docs/transformations/#share-bundles">documented API</a
          > and original sources.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Review-only candidates are not automatically transformed. Share Bundle preparation is a
    separate, explicit API operation, not an automatic step after transformation.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

